.TH QORE-DATA-PROVIDER-I18N 1 "2026 October 24" "Qore 3.0" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
qore\-data\-provider\-i18n \- extract source-owned data-provider presentation catalogs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qore\-data\-provider\-i18n
.BR \-o " " \fIdirectory\fP
[\fIoptions\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBqore\-data\-provider\-i18n\fR extracts application, action, option, and
allowed-value presentation metadata registered by data-provider modules,
including the fields reachable through option types.  The extracted texts are
labels, short and long descriptions, and the plain-words descriptions of the
values that option and field validation patterns accept; validation patterns,
example values, and other technical values are not extracted.  It
writes Qore native root catalogs whose message identifiers derive only from
exact technical identities.  The generated catalogs can therefore be
translated without changing provider application, action, option, or value
identifiers.
.PP
One file is written for each catalog domain as
\fIdirectory/domain/root.json\fR.  Existing files are replaced unless
\fB\-\-check\fR is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIdirectory\fP
Root catalog output directory.  This option is required.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-module =\fImodule\fP
Load a provider module before extraction.  Repeat for multiple modules.
.TP
.BR \-\-owner =\fImodule\fP
Load a provider module and extract only the app and action presentation
contributions registered by that module.  Repeat for multiple owner modules.
Transitive and ambient modules are excluded.  This is the deterministic form
for source-owned module catalogs, including modules that contribute actions to
an app owned by another module.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-app =\fIapp\fP
Extract an exact registered application identifier.  Repeat for multiple
applications.  If omitted and
.B \-\-owner
is not used, all applications registered in the process are extracted.
.TP
.BR \-\-check
Do not write files.  Exit with status 2 if a generated root catalog is missing
or differs semantically from the checked-in file.  Every discovered sibling
translation is also checked for a canonical locale filename, a valid native
catalog shape, current producer source text, and message identifiers that are
still present in the generated root catalog.  Partial translations and
translated text identical to the producer text remain valid.
When
.B \-\-app
is omitted, the check also rejects catalog domains in the output directory
that are not present in the generated catalog set.
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-tree
Recursively find and validate all source-owned provider catalogs below the
output directory without loading provider modules.  This validates native
catalog structure and translation provenance for Qore, external module, and
third-party catalog trees without a provider or locale list.  It cannot compare root
catalogs to provider metadata; use
.B \-\-check
in the provider's source repository for that check.
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-source\-tree
Recursively discover catalogs in canonical
.I Module/i18n
and
.I Module.i18n
source layouts, discover Qore modules containing exact data-provider
registration calls even before their first catalog exists, load every
technical owner module, and compare each root and translation with current
provider metadata.  Owner modules are inferred from the source layout and
technical registration APIs without provider, application, or locale lists.  Use
.B \-\-owner
to identify the owner of a noncanonical source tree; exactly one owner is
required when it cannot be inferred.  Use
.B \-m
only to load any additional runtime dependency.
.TP
.BR \-\-update\-source\-tree
Discover the root catalogs and owner modules below the output directory as
.B \-\-check\-source\-tree
does, load every owner module once, and rewrite every root catalog from the
current provider metadata.  Translations are not changed.
.TP
.BR \-\-rekey\-source\-tree
Discover the catalogs and owner modules below the output directory as
.B \-\-check\-source\-tree
does and move every catalog to the message identifiers of the current
provider metadata, carrying its translations.  Each root catalog is rewritten
from the current metadata; in each translation file, a translation is kept for
the new identifier of its message when the producer text there is unchanged.
The fields of a type reached below the options of an action have one message
for each text in that action, however many options or paths reach the type;
catalogs whose messages identified such a type by the option and path that
reached it have one message for each of them, and these come together.  When
they had different translations of one text, the translation given most often
is kept, or the first one in the file for a tie, and the text is reported as a
variant.  A message without such a translation takes the translation that the
locale gives the same text of the same field and member under another
identifier, if there is exactly one.  For each domain that changes, a
.B REKEY:
line gives the number of messages before and after and the numbers of
translations carried, variants, translations reused by text, missing
translations, and new texts, which are texts the old root catalog did not
have.  Only the
.I domain/root.json
layout is supported.
.IP
If two types reached below the options of one action have the same name,
shape, schema path and schema identity but give a field different texts,
extraction is refused for the owner module, which is reported as a conflict.  If any domain has a
conflict, nothing is written, and the exit status is 2.
.TP
.BR \-\-mechanical
With
.BR \-\-rekey\-source\-tree ,
re-key the committed root catalogs instead of loading the owner modules: the
messages of a type reached below the options of an action are given their
per-action identifiers, and messages that come together must have the same
producer text, or they are reported as a conflict.  No other identifier
changes.  No module is loaded, so
.B \-m
and
.B \-\-owner
cannot be given.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
With
.BR \-\-rekey\-source\-tree ,
report what would be re-keyed and write nothing.
.TP
.BR \-\-require\-standard\-locales
With a check mode, require a translation file for every standard translation
locale.
.TP
.BR \-\-require\-complete\-locales
With a check mode, require every checked translation file to translate every
root message.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show loaded modules and written files.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Extract the built-in Qore provider catalog:
.RS
.B qore\-data\-provider\-i18n \-o qlib/DataProvider/i18n \-a Qore
.RE
.PP
Verify a module's checked-in catalogs:
.RS
.B qore\-data\-provider\-i18n \-\-check \-o qlib/json.i18n \-\-owner json
.RE
.PP
Verify every provider catalog below an installed or source tree:
.RS
.B qore\-data\-provider\-i18n \-\-check\-tree \-o qlib
.RE
.PP
Verify every provider catalog against its source owner modules:
.RS
.B qore\-data\-provider\-i18n \-\-check\-source\-tree \-o qlib
.RE
.PP
Report how the catalogs of a source tree would be re-keyed, then re-key them:
.RS
.B qore\-data\-provider\-i18n \-\-rekey\-source\-tree \-\-dry\-run \-o .
.br
.B qore\-data\-provider\-i18n \-\-rekey\-source\-tree \-o .
.RE
